      "title": "Employee eligibility",
      "narration": "Priya’s plan defines who may enroll. Employees must be in an eligible class, typically full-time workers averaging 30 or more hours a week, and must be actively at work when coverage begins. New hires usually serve a probationary, or waiting, period before becoming eligible; federal law caps it at 90 days. When the waiting period ends, the employee has an eligibility period, usually 31 days, to enroll without evidence of insurability. An employee who misses it is a late enrollee and may have to wait for the next open enrollment. Part-time employees may be included at the employer’s option under Maryland’s small group rules.",
