      "title": "Open and special enrollment",
      "narration": "Once a year the plan holds an annual open enrollment, when any eligible employee may join or change coverage without a qualifying event. Between open enrollments, HIPAA’s special enrollment periods allow entry after a loss of other coverage, marriage, birth, adoption or placement, if requested within 30 days, and after a change in Medicaid or children’s health program eligibility, within 60 days. Priya’s employee who waived coverage because of her husband’s plan may join within 30 days when he loses his job. Outside these windows the plan may make a late enrollee wait, though it may not exclude conditions.",
