      "title": "Coordination of benefits at work",
      "narration": "Group plans include the coordination of benefits provision from Lesson 23. For an employee covered under two group plans, the plan covering her as an employee is primary. For a dependent child, the birthday rule applies, or the custodial parent’s plan when parents are divorced without a decree. The secondary plan pays the remaining allowable expense up to its own benefit, so payments never exceed the bill. Employers ask about other coverage at enrollment because COB savings lower the group’s claims. An employee who conceals a spouse’s plan may have claims reprocessed and benefits recovered.",
